      "message": "NamedTemporaryFile creates the file on disk and holds an open handle.\n\nInside try:, open(test_conf, \"w\") opens the file again while f_test_config from the context manager has closed (or is still closing depending on OS).\n\nMore importantly, using NamedTemporaryFile(delete\u003dFalse) means the file is never unlinked if build_zephyr completes successfully without throwing an exception!\n\nThe except Exception: block unlinks test_conf on failure.\n\nbuild() cleans it up in its finally: block only if build() gets called. But if build_zephyr is called directly or returns normally, the file remains on disk for successful builds.\n\nRemediation:\nKeep NamedTemporaryFile open and write directly into it using its file object rather than reopening it by path, or ensure cleanup occurs reliably in all control paths:\n\n```\nwith tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(\n    mode\u003d\"w\",\n    encoding\u003d\"utf-8\",\n    prefix\u003d\"test-\",\n    suffix\u003d\".conf\",\n    delete\u003dFalse,\n) as f_test_config:\n    test_conf \u003d f_test_config.name\n    cmd \u003d cmd + [\"-DOVERLAY_CONFIG\u003d\" + test_conf]\n    \n    # Write configuration directly to f_test_config without reopening:\n    testcase_path \u003d os.path.join(ZEPHYR_FPMCU_DIR, \"testcase.yaml\")\n    ...\n    ```",
